Accept any QMI port when looking for the modem, not just a port named
"qrtr0".

81voltd was written for QRTR-transport devices (pmOS), where ModemManager
exposes the modem QMI port as "qrtr0". On msm8916 boards with bam-dmux the
same modem is exposed as "wwan0qmi0", so the daemon warned
"ModemManager QRTR modem not detected on startup" and never handled any
IMS Data request. The daemon does not open QMI itself (it only creates
bearers through ModemManager), so the port name is irrelevant; the QMI
port type is the correct discriminator.

--- a/qvd-modem.c
+++ b/qvd-modem.c
@@ -206,8 +206,7 @@
 	mm_modem_peek_ports(modem, &ports, &n_ports);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < n_ports; i++) {
-		if (ports[i].type == MM_MODEM_PORT_TYPE_QMI
-		 && !strcmp(ports[i].name, "qrtr0")) {
+		if (ports[i].type == MM_MODEM_PORT_TYPE_QMI) {
 			is_qrtr = TRUE;
 			break;
 		}
@@ -278,8 +277,7 @@
 	mm_modem_peek_ports(modem, &ports, &n_ports);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < n_ports; i++) {
-		if (ports[i].type == MM_MODEM_PORT_TYPE_QMI
-		 && !strcmp(ports[i].name, "qrtr0")) {
+		if (ports[i].type == MM_MODEM_PORT_TYPE_QMI) {
 			is_qrtr = TRUE;
 			break;
 		}
